1 OCCU Bendahara Seri Maharaja (1722 - 1736)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tun Abbas  (Bendahara Seri Maharaja Pahang).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Y.M. Sri Paduka Tun Abbas ibni al-Marhum Sultan ‘Abdu’l Jalil Ri’ayat Shah, Dato’ Bendahara SriMaharaja (cre. 4th October 1722). b. ca. 1698, educ. privately. Appointed as Governor of Pahang by his father in 1719. Styled Dato’ 
2 CONC Temenggong Sri Maharaja 1721-1722. He went mad and d. at Bulang, 1736, having had issue: a) Y.M. Sri Paduka Tun ‘Abdu’l Jamal bin Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaja Tun Abbas, Dato’Temenggong Paduka Raja of Riau (cre. 1757). He became m
2 CONC entally unstable and killed his nephew, Tun ‘Abdu’l Mutalib, in a fit of jealousy at Kuala Pahang in 1802. Arrested on the orders of the Sultan and sent as a prisoner to Riau. m. (first) Y.M. Tuan Encik Lah binti Dato’ Temenggong 
2 CONC Tun Mutahir, of Pasir Naring, daughter of his paternal uncle, Y.M. Tun Muhammad Tahir ibni al-Marhum Sultan ‘Abdu’l Jalil [Mutahir], Dato’ Temenggong Sri Maharaja, by his second wife, Encik Che’ Puan, daughter of Y.M. Sri Paduka T
2 CONC un Muhammad Kamil [Mukamil] bin Dato’ Bendahara ‘Abdu’l Majid, Dato’ Temenggong Sri Maharaja, of Tanjong Batu. m. (second) ca. 1740, Daeng Maimuna (b. ca. 1723; d. after 1795), daughter of Opu Daeng Parani bin Opu Ten-ri Burang Da
2 CONC eng Rilaga, by his second wife, Y.A.M. Tengku Tengah Fatima binti al-Marhum Sultan ‘Abdu’l Jalil Ri’ayat Shah, daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan ‘Abdu’l Jalil IV Ri’ayat Shah Zillu’llah fi al-’Alam bin Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaj
2 CONC a Tun Habib Ghazi, Sultan of Johor and Pahang. He was k. with his two sons in an explosion on a boat at Bulang, 1803, having had issue, five sons and two daughters.
