1 TITL Yang Dipertuan Muda Riau IV, Marhum Teluk Ketapang
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raja_Haji_Fisabilillah Wikipedia]
2 CONT Raja Haji Fisabilillah (full name Raja Haji Fisabilillah ibni Daeng Chelak) (1727 – 18 June 1784) was a Bugis-Malay warrior, and also the 4th Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Riau from 1777 to 1784.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1777 - 1784 Y.M. Paduka Sri Raja Haji bin Raja Chelak [Raja Haji al-Shahid Fisabillu'llah Ta'ala al-Marhum Teluk Ketapang], Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Riau, eldest son of Y.M. Paduka Sri Raja Chelak bin Daing Rilaga, Yang di-Pertuan 
2 CONC Muda of Riau, by his first wife, Encik Tomita. Granted the title of Engku Kelana Jaya Putra 1748. Granted the title of Pangeran Suta Vijaya by the Sultan of Jambi, February 1760. Installed at Pahang, 1778. m. (first) at Selangor, 
2 CONC 1748, Y.M. Tun Encik Aisha binti Tun Engku Kelana Encik Unuk (d. shortly after her marriage), daughter of Y.M. Opu La Mupa Unuk, Tun Engku Kelana Encik Unuk, by his wife, a Kedah princess. m. (second) after 1748, Y.M. Raja Amaran 
2 CONC binti al-Marhum Tuanku Muhammad Mahrum Shah, Ungku Encik Sejuk, daughter of Sri Paduka Tuanku Muhammad Mahrum Shah ibni al-Marhum Tuanku Saidi Shah [al-Marhum Gagap], Raja and Yang di-Pertuan of Asahan. m. (third) at Pedas, 1758, 
2 CONC Y.M. Raja Fatima binti Daing Kamboja, Tengku Raja Perak, eldest daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Daing Kamboja bin Opu Daing Parani, Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Riau, by his second wife, 'Ungku Tua. m. (fourth) before 1760, Y.M. Raja Halim
2 CONC a binti al-Marhum Sultan Saleh ud-din Karamat Shah [Encik Gaong], daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Hasan Saleh ud-din Karamat Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Muzafar Shah, Sultan of Indragiri. m. (fifth) before 1769, Encik Gandira, a
2 CONC  lady from Indragiri. m. (sixth) at Jambi, February 1760, Y.A.M. Ratu Mas Deva (d. at Jambi, shortly after her son), daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Sri ing Alaga 'Abdu'l Rahman ibni al-Marhum Sultan Anum Sri ing Alaga 'Abdu'l 
2 CONC Mahji Muhammad Shafi, Sultan of Jambi. m. (seventh) Encik Upay, a lady from Riau. m. (eighth) Encik Uning, a lady from Indragiri. m. (ninth) 1778, Encik Mariam, a lady from Riau. He was k. in battle at Tanjong Palas, Malacca, 19th
2 CONC  June 1784 (bur. St Paul's Hill, Malacca, later moved to Penyengat Island), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: Riau4
2 CONT --------------------
