1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Abdul Jalil Mu'azzam Syah VI  (Sultan Johor-Riau ke14; 1760-61).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1760 - 1761 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil V Mu'azzam Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Sulaiman Badr ul-'Alam Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Johor and Pahang and their dependencies. b. 11th March 1738, second son of H.H
2 CONC . Paduka Sri Sultan Sulaiman Badr ul-'Alam Shah Khalifat ul-Muminim ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Ri'ayat Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Johor and Pahang and their dependencies, by his first wife, Encik Puan Perak
2 CONC , educ. privately. Styled Raja di-Baroh before his accession. Installed as Heir Apparent with the title of Raja Muda, October 1759. Succeeded on the death of his father, 1760. m. H.H. Tengku Puteh binti Raja Chelak (d. at Batangan
2 CONC , February 1761), daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Raja Chelak bin Opu Ten-ri Burang Daing Rilaga, Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Riau, by his wife, H.H. Tengku Mandak binti al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Ri'ayat Shah, Tengku, daughter of H.H
2 CONC . Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil IV Ri'ayat Shah Zillu'llah fi al-'Alam bin Dato' Bendahara Sri Maharaja Tun Habib Ghazi, Sultan of Johor and Pahang. He d. (poisoned?) at Kuala Selangor, 29th January 1761 (bur. Batangan), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: Jojor4
