2 CONT 1826 - 1831 H.H. Paduka Sri Tuanku Raja Labuh, Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Negri Sembilan, grandson (according to his credentials, not son) of the Yang di-Pertuan of Pagaruyung – see Newbold pp 85-86. Sent by the Kalifatu’llah Yang d
2 CONC i-Pertuan Sakti of Minangkabau at the invitation of a party of the Minangkabau nobles of Negri Sembilan, 1826. Deposed and expelled by the Undang Lauts for his association with Raja Kerjan, 30th November 1831. Went into exile to M
2 CONC alacca and finally crossed over the straits to Telapak Burok in Siak in 1832. m. at Sungai Ujong, 1828, Y.M. Tunku Hitam binti al-Marhum Sultan Muhammad Shah, widow of Y.M. TunkuiSeh, and younger daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Muhamm
2 CONC ad Shah ibni al-Marhum Raja Adil, Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Rembau. He had issue, several children. 
