2 CONT 1808 - 1830 H.H. Paduka Sri Tuanku Sultan Ahmad Shah I ibni al-Marhum Sultan Zainal-Abidin [al-Marhum Parit], Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Trengganu, eldest son of H.H. Paduka Sri Tuanku Sultan Zainal-Abidin II ibni al-Marh
2 CONC um Sultan Mansur Riayat, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Trengganu, by his first wife, Inche' Wan Zainab, Cik Puan Besar, educ. privately. Proclaimed on the death of his father, 1808. m. (first) Perempuan Cina, a Chinese lady.
2 CONC  m. (second) before 1808, Y.A.M. Tengku Putri binti al-Marhum Sultan Mahmud Shah Alam, Tengku Besar Perempuan, daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri al-Wakil al-Imam Sultan Mahmud Ri'ayat Shah Zilu'llah fil'Alam Khalifat ul-Muminin ibni al-
2 CONC Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Johor and Pahang. m. (third) Cik Hajar binti 'Abdu'llah, Cik Puan Besar (bur. Perkuboran Sheikh Ibrahim, Kuala Trengganu), second daughter of a travelling Chine
2 CONC se Minora player from Patani. He d. at Parit, 4th July 1830 (bur. Sheikh Ibrahim Cemetery, Kuala Trengganu), having had issue, four sons and four daughters.
2 CONT
