2 CONC aji [Engku Talluk] (d/o Raja Amaran). m. (first) 177x, Y.M. Raja Nala ibni al-Marhum Sultan Saleh ud-din, Raja Muda (d. at Aceh, Sumatra, 1795), second son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Saleh ud-din Shah ibni al-Marhum Raja Chelak, Su
2 CONC ltan of Selangor. She had issue, one son - see Malaysia (Selangor). m. (second) a Y.M. Raja of Asahan?
2 CONT
2 CONT =3) Y.M. Raja Siti binti Raja Haji [Engku Besar] (d/o Raja Fatima). m. at Lawar, Borneo, 1788, Karaeng Taliba Sultan 'Ali [Engku Karaeng Talibak], Datu of Pammana (d. in Sulewesi, 9th February 1822), grandson of Datu-ri Watu. She 
2 CONC d. at Penyengat Island, after April 1827, by whom she had issue, an only daughter - see Indonesia (Pammana).=
2 CONT '''' Copyright© Christopher Buyers 4) Y.M. Raja Hamida binti Raja Haji [Engku Putri]. b. after 1758 (d/o Raja Fatima). She refused to surrender the Johor regalia after the death of her husband, thereby forestalling the installatio
2 CONC n of any of his sons. m. at Riau, 1803, as his fourth wife, H.H. Paduka Sri al-Wakil al-Imam Sultan Mahmud Ri'ayat Shah Zilu'llah fil'Alam Khalifat ul-Muminin ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Be
2 CONC sar of Johor and Pahang (b. 24th March 1756; d. at Fort Tanna, Bukit Chengah, Lingga, 12th January 1811, bur. Masjid Jami', Daik), younger son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil V Mu'azzam Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Sulaiman 
2 CONC Badr ul-'Alam Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Johor and Pahang, by his wife, H.H. Tengku Puteh binti Raja Chelak, third daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Raja Chelak bin Opu Ten-ri Burang Daing Rilaga, Yang di-Pertuan Muda of 
2 CONC Riau. She d. at Kota Ranteng, Penyengat Island, Riau, 5th August 1844 (bur. there), having had issue, an only daughter - see Malaysia (Johor). 5) Y.M. Raja Buntit binti Raja Haji [Encik Tengku] (d/o Raja Halima). m. Y.M. Encik Ung
2 CONC ku Raja Sulaiman bin Arung Lingga (b. 1767; d. before 1824), son of Daing Lakani, Arung Lingga, by his wife, Y.M. Raja Amina binti Raja Chelak, eldest daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Raja Chelak bin Daing Rilaga, Yang di-Pertuan Muda 
2 CONC of Riau. She d. at Daik, Lingga, after April 1827, having had issue, two daughters - see above. 6) H.H. Raja Tengah binti Raja Haji, Tengku Ampuan. b. before 30th June 1764 (d/o Raja Halima). m. at Lingga, 1796, H.H. Paduka Sri Su
2 CONC ltan Ibrahim Shah ibni Sultan Saleh ud-din, Sultan of Selangor (b. ca. 1736; d. 27th October 1826), eldest son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Saleh ud-din Shah ibni al-Marhum Raja Chelak, Sultan of Selangor, by his first wife, the Engk
2 CONC u Puan, a younger daughter of Paduka Sri Sultan 'Ala ud-din Ri'ayat Shah bin Daing Rilaga, Yang di-Pertuan Muda of Riau. She d. at Penyengat Island, after April 1827, having had issue, an only son - see Malaysia (Selangor). 7) Y.M
2 CONC . Raja Amina binti Raja Haji (d/o Encik Upay). She d. unm. at Penyengat Island, after April 1827. 8) Y.M. Raja Pasir binti Raja Haji (d/o a junior wife). m. (div.) H.H. al-Wathiq billah Paduka Sri Sultan Said Jamal ud-din Mudayat 
2 CONC Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Ibrahim, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Indragiri (b. ca. 1794; d. at Istana Rengat, 29th May 1876, and bur. there at the Masjid Raya), second son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Ibrahim II Bahar ud-din A
2 CONC lam Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Indragiri. She d.s.p. at Penyengat Island, after April 1827- see Indonesia (Indragiri). Copyright© Christopher Buyers continued on the next page.
