1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1760-1761 and 1779-1781 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Ismail 'Abdu'l Jalil Jalal ud-din Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mahmud 'Abdu'l Jalil Jalal ud-din Muzaffar Shah [al-Marhum Mankat di-Balai], Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Be
2 CONC sar of Siak Sri Indrapura. b. before 1746, eldest son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Mahmud 'Abdu'l Jalil Jalal ud-din Muzaffar Shah, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Siak Sri Indrapura, by his second wife, Daing Metho, 'Ungku Puan,
2 CONC  educ. privately. Appointed Yang di-Pertuan Raja Muda by his father. Raised to the throne by the nobles of Siak on the death of his father, in contravention of a manifesto, which appointed his brother, Raja Musa as his successor, 
2 CONC 23rd November 1760. Expelled by his elder brother and fled to Palembang, 16th January 1761. Settled in Trengganu 1764-1779. Returned to Siak with a large force and after investing the city for three days, succeeded in re-establish
2 CONC ing himself on the throne, 19th August 1779. He lost his reason soon afterwards and was placed under supervision. m. (first) before 1760, Y.A.M. Tengku Sani binti Tengku Busu, elder daughter of his paternal uncle, Y.A.M. Tengku Ib
2 CONC rahim ibni al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l Jalil Rahmad Shah [Tengku Busu], sometime Presdt. of the Family Cncl. m. (second) at Kuala Trengganu, March 1764, Y.A.M. Tengku Neh binti al-Marhum Sultan Mansur Shah [Tun Tipah], fifth daughter
2 CONC  of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Mansur Shah I ibni al-Marhum Sultan Zainal-Abidin, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Trengganu. m. (third) a commoner. m. (fourth) a commoner. m. (fifth) a commoner. He d. at Kudung, 31st July 1781, 
2 CONT
