1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sultan Kelantan 1837-86.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Long Senik bin Long Tan Aria Pahlawan bergelar Yang di Pertuan  Kelantan 1838-1845. Baginda terkenali juga dgn nama Long Senik Kampung Sirih atau Long Senik Mulut Merah. Memerintah Negeri Kelantan dengan gelaran Sultan Mohd II ata
2 CONC u Sultan Mulut Merah dalam tahun 1845-1886. Setelah mangkat ada kalanya digelar Marhum Tua. (Lawatan Abdullah Munshi ke Negeri Kelantan dalam tahun 1838 ada cerita tentang perang saudara kerana perebutan takhta) Long Tan Aria Pahl
2 CONC awan terbunuh di Galas, Ulu Kelantan.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1835 - 1886 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad II ibni al-Marhum Tengku Temenggong Long Tan [Sultan Mulut Merah], Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan. b. ca. 1794, as Long Senik, fourth son of Tengku Long Tan ib
2 CONC ni al-Marhum Sultan Long Yunus, Tengku Temenggong Aria Pahlawan, educ. privately. Adopted by his childless uncle, Sultan Muhammad I. Raised to the title of Tengku Temenggong Aria Pahlawan and appointed as Heir Presumptive, after t
2 CONC he death of his father. Succeeded on the death of his uncle and adopted father, as Raja and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan, 26th January 1835. As a consequence of dissension within the Royal Family, he was obliged,
2 CONC  by virtue of a Siamese compromise, to share power with his uncle, Tengku Long Zainal. The latter styled Yang di-Pertuan Muda and Muhammad Yang di-Pertuan Besar. Recognised as ruler by the King of Siam and raised to the title of P
2 CONC haya Visit Bakdiya 1836, and prom. to Phraya Deva Kelantan 1845. Raised to the title of Phraya Devanujitha Mahesvara Rajanukula Vibunlaya Bakdiya Sri Sultan Muhammad Rattanathada Mahapaddana Adikara (Phraya Dechanuchitmahitsarajan
2 CONC ukulawibunlayaphakdi Seri Sultan Muhammad Rattanathada Mahapathanathikan) by King Rama V of Siam 4th March 1877. m. H.H. Sultana Batoh [To'] binti Tengku Long Yusuf [Tuan Besar], granted the title of Tengku Ampuan, and later promo
2 CONC ted to Sultana in March 1877, youngest daughter of Y.B.M. Tengku Long Yusuf ibni al-Marhum Sultan Long Yunus, of Bukit Panjor. He d. at the Istana Balai Besar, Kota Bahru, 30th October 1886 (bur. Royal Cemetery, Kampung Langgar). 
2 CONC He had two sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============================================
2 CONT 1835 - 1886 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad II ibni al-Marhum Tengku Temenggong Long Tan [Sultan Mulut Merah], Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan.
2 CONT
2 CONT b. ca. 1794, as Long Senik, fourth son of Tengku Long Tan ibni al-Marhum Sultan Long Yunus, Tengku Temenggong Aria Pahlawan,
2 CONT
2 CONT educ. privately.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adopted by his childless uncle, Sultan Muhammad I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raised to the title of Tengku Temenggong Aria Pahlawan 25th June 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebelled against his cousin, attacked his fort and attempted to assume supreme authority, 25th August 1835. As a consequence of continuing dissension within the Royal Family, he was obliged, by virtue of a Siamese compromise, to s
2 CONC hare power with his uncle, Tengku Long Zainal. The latter styled Yang di-Pertuan Muda; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhammad being styled Raja and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Kelantan ca July 1838. Recognised as ruler by the King of Siam and raised to the title of Phaya Visit Bakdiya Sri Sultan Muhammad Ratna Nuchitra Sri Sundhana Buwanabakdi Varm
2 CONC an Phya Kelantan  (Pipitpakdi Sri Sultan Muhammad Ratna Nuchit Siti Santun Bua (or Bru) Bahdi Wangsa Pia Kelantan) April 1839, and prom to Phraya Deva Kelantan 1845. Raised to the title of Phraya Dejanujitha Mahesvara Rajanukula V
2 CONC ibunlayabakdi Sri Sultan Muhammad Rattanathada Mahapadhana Adikara of Muang Kelantan (Phraya Dechanuchit Mahitsa Rajanukula Wibunlaya Phakdi Seri Sultan Muhammad Rattanathada Mahapathanathikan Pusamkan Mebun Kelantan) by King Rama
2 CONC  V of Siam 4th March 1877. Thereafter assumed the style of Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan.
2 CONT
2 CONT m. (first) H.H. Sultana Batoh [To’] binti Tuan Long Yusuf [Tuan Besar], granted the title of Tengku Ampuan, and later promoted to Sultana 4th March 1877, youngest daughter of Y.M. Tuan Long Yusuf ibni al-Marhum Sultan Long Yunus, 
2 CONC of Bukit Panjor. m. (second) Y.M. Engku Putri Neng binti Engku Long Sri, Raja Perempuan Gunung (d. at Kota Bharu, before 9th August 1873; bur. Langgar Limbat, Pasir Tumboh), daughter of Y.M. Engku Long Sri bin Tuan Long Gaffar, Te
2 CONC ngku Sri Maharaja, of Jeram. m. (third) Nik Embong. m. (fourth?) Ku Senik Tendong, Raja Perempuan II.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. at the Istana Balai Besar, Kota Bharu, 30th October 1886 (bur. there at the Royal Cemetery, Langgar), having had issue, two sons and one daughter:
