1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Installed by Sultan Sultan Mahmud Ri'ayat Shah, at Lingga, before 11th March 1807. A staunch supporter of Sultan Husain over the claims of his half-brother, the Dutch candidate, 'Abdu'l Rahman. He befriended Sir Th
2 CONC omas Stamford Raffles, by whom he was encouraged to settle in Singapore with Sultan Husain, where he was instrumental in arranging the cession of the island to the British on 6th January 1819. Granted the hereditary style of His H
2 CONC ighness by the British 30th January 1819. He died at Teluk Belanga, Singapore, 8th December 1825 (bur. there at the Temenggong Mausoleum, Teluk Belanga Mosque), having had issue, two sons and four daughters:
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Temenggung Daeng Kecil Daik (Temenggung Tun Ibrahim). Temenggung Johor.
