3 CTRY Malaysia
1 OCCU Paduka Sri Sultan of Kelantan (1886 - 1890)
1 TITL Al Marhum Sultan Ahmad Tengah
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Raja Kelantan 1886-9 (putera Terengganu).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lg Sulung b Lg Senik bergelar Sultan Ahmad  dalam tahun 1886-1889.  Dikenali juga dgn nama Long Ahmad atau Long Sulong.  Setelah mangkat digelar Sultan Tengah atau Marhum Tengah. Jalan-jalan darat mula dibuat dari Kota Bharu ke Pu
2 CONC lai Chondong dan sampai ke Kuala Krai dalam tahun 1908 yang sebelum ini bergantung kepada hanya melalui Sungai Kelantan.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1886 - 1890 H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Ahmad ibni al-Marhum Muhammad [Sultan Tengah], Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan, eldest son of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan Muhammad II ibni al-Marhum Tengku Temenggong Long Ta
2 CONC n, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan, educ. privately. Raised to the title of Tengku Besar by his father, and Phya Rajadadhipati Putrapurutravisesa (Phra Ratsathibodi Butburutphiset) by King Rama IV of Siam
2 CONC  1860. Appointed as Siamese Governor over Kelantan, prom. to the title of Phraya Rajadipati Putrapurutravisesa Pradisvara Rajanarubadindra Surindra Ravivamsa (Phraya Ratsathibodi Butburutphiset Prathetsaratchanarubodin Surintharaw
2 CONC iwangsa) and presented with a Sword of Honour, 14th June 1869. Succeeded on the death of his father, 30th October 1886. Installed as Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of the State of Kelantan on the same day. He died at Istana Jaha
2 CONC r, Kota Bahru, 8th March1890 (buried at the Royal Cemetery, Kampung Langgar).He had sixteen sons and thirteen daughters:
