1 NAME Tengku Temenggung Tengku Abdul Ghaffar
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Y.B.M. Tengku Long ‘Abdu’l Ja’afar ibni al-Marhum Sultan Muhammad II [Tuan Long Ghaffar], Tengku Temenggong *. b. at Kota Bharu, 29th September 1875 (s/o Ku Senik Tendong), educ. privately. Granted the title of Ten
2 CONC gku Petra di-Dalam Kebun 1900, and prom to Tengku Temenggong ca. 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Granted the title of Phra Bidaksha Dejanaratta (Phra Bitak Detcha Rat) by the King of Siam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Actg Cmasnr of Police 1904, Port Officer 1907-1910, Sec 1910-1930, MSC 1921-1935. Founder Kampung Temenggung Arts Centre in 1923. Lived for some years in Senggora, Siam. Rcvd: Silver Jubilee Medal (1935).
2 CONT
2 CONT m. (first) Y.M. Tengku Kembang binti Tuan Long Nik, daughter of Y.M. Tuan Long Nik bin Engku Long Mansur [Lonik], of Tapong. m. (second) Cik Zainab [Mak Nab Raja]. m. (third) Hajjah Sofiah binti Marak [Mak Tuan].
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. at Che Hir, near Tak Bai, Thailand, 3rd May 1935 (bur. Royal Cemetery, Langgar, Kota Bharu), having had issue, two sons and two daughters:
