1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Temenggung Ibrahim (Daeng Ronggek). Temenggung Singapura & Johor (Sultan Johor ke-20) 1855-62).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Tun Ibrahim bin Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Daing 'Abdu'l Rahman, Maharaja of Johor. born on the island of Bulan, in the Riau archipelago, 8th December 1810, younger son of Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaj
2 CONC a Daing 'Abdu'l Rahman bin Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Tun 'Abdu'l Hamid, by his first wife, Encik Yah, educated privately in Singapore. Acted for his elder brother from 1833. Replaced him as Sri Paduka Dato Temenggong Sri Mahara
2 CONC ja, and installed at New Harbour, Singapore, 19th August 1841. Presented with the ceremonial sword of the Sultans of Johor in the presence of the Sultan of Johor, the Sultan of Lingga and Tuanku Ja'afar, by the Governor of the Str
2 CONC aits Settlements, 31st August 1846. Installed as hereditary ruler of Johor with the title of Maharaja of Johor, and granted a hereditary salute of 11-guns, 10th March 1855. 
2 CONT
2 CONT married. (first) before 1832, Encik Ngah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT married. (second) Engku Long Muda. 
2 CONT
2 CONT married. (third) before 1841, Tengku Andak binti Sultan 'Abdu'l-Rahman Mu'azzam Shah, third daughter of Sultan 'Abdu'l Rahman I Mu'azzam Shah ibni Sultan Mahmud Shah Alam, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Lingga, Riau and its d
2 CONC ependencies. He died at Teluk Belanga, Singapore, 31st January 1862 (bur. there at the Temenggong Mausoleum, Teluk Belanga Mosque), having had issue, seven sons and five daughters: 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1855 - 1862 H.H. Sri Paduka Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Tun Ibrahim bin Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Daing 'Abdu'l Rahman, Maharaja of Johor. b. on the island of Bulan, in the Riau archipelago, 8th December 1810, younger son of H
2 CONC .H. Sri Paduka Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Daing 'Abdu'l Rahman bin Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja Tun 'Abdu'l Hamid, by his first wife, Encik Yah, educ. privately in Singapore. Acted for his elder brother from 1833. Replaced him a
2 CONC s Sri Paduka Dato Temenggong Sri Maharaja, and installed at New Harbour, Singapore, 19th August 1841. Presented with the ceremonial sword of the Sultans of Johor in the presence of the Sultan of Johor, the Sultan of Lingga and Tua
2 CONC nku Ja'afar, by the Governor of the Straits Settlements, 31st August 1846. Installed as hereditary ruler of Johor with the title of Maharaja of Johor, and granted a hereditary salute of 11-guns, 10th March 1855. m. (first) before 
2 CONC 1832, Encik Ngah. m. (second) Engku Long Muda. m. (third) before 1841, H.H. Tengku Andak binti al-Marhum Sultan 'Abdu'l-Rahman Mu'azzam Shah, third daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan 'Abdu'l Rahman I Mu'azzam Shah ibni al-Marhum S
2 CONC ultan Mahmud Shah Alam, Sultan and Yang di-Pertuan Besar of Lingga, Riau and its dependencies. He d. at Teluk Belanga, Singapore, 31st January 1862 (bur. there at the Temenggong Mausoleum, Teluk Belanga Mosque), having had issue, 
2 CONC seven sons and five daughters:
