1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1858 – 1863 H.H. Sri Paduka Tun Muhammad Tahir bin Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaja Tun ‘Ali [Bendahara Tua], Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaja of Pahang. b. 1813, eldest son of H.H. Sri Paduka Tun ‘Ali ibni al-Marhum Dato’
2 CONC  Bendahara Paduka Raja Tun Koris, Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaja of Pahang, by his first wife, Encik Wan Ngah, educ. privately. Appointed as Heir Apparent and invested with the title of Engku Muda Dato’ Bendahara Sri Wak Raja 1847. 
2 CONC Succeeded his father as Sri Paduka Dato’ Bendahara Sri Maharaja, October 1858. Transferred most of his administrative functions to his eldest son after he became incapacitated by old age, May 1861. m. (first) ca 1823, Y.A.M. Tengk
2 CONC u Kechil binti al-Marhum Sultan ‘Abdu’l-Rahman Mu’azzam Shah [Tengku Chit], eldest daughter of H.H. Paduka Sri Sultan ‘Abdu’r Rahman I Mu’adzam Shah ibni al-Marhum Sultan Mahmud Shah Alam, Sultan of Lingga, Riau and its dependenci
2 CONC es. m. (second) 1832, Y.A.M. Tunku Chik binti al-Marhum Sultan Ahmad Taj ud-din Halim Shah, daughter of H.H. Maulana Paduka Sri Sultan Ahmad Taj ud-din Halim Shah I ibni al-Marhum ‘Abdu’llah al-Mukarram Shah, Sultan of Kedah, by h
2 CONC is wife, Che’ Arshid. He d. at sea, while sailing to Singapore, near Kuala Sedili, 30th May 1863 (bur. at Bukit Timbalan, Johor Bahru), having had issue, eight sons and four daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: [http://www.royalark.net/Malaysia/pahang5.htm]
