0 @N6000000006450106537@ NOTE (Research):Proclaimed at Kota Tinggi on the death of Sultan Mahmud Shah II of Johor as Paduka Sri Sultan ' Abdu'l Jalil Ri'ayat Shah, 3rd September 1699. Fled from Johore Lama following rebellion against his brother, the yang di-P
1 CONC ertuan Muda, 1712. Captured by Raja Kechil, putative son of the deceased Sultan Mahammad Shah 11, 21st March 1717. He was then reappointed to the post of Dato' Bendahara Sri Maharaja, and lived at Kota Tinggi. Retired to Pahang 17
1 CONC 19, and to Trengganu 1720. Established a new capital at Kuala Pahang, 11th July 1721.
1 CONT He was killed on board his ship by an emissary sent by Raja Kechil, while conducting his prayers, before 21st November 1721.
